<!--
  ============================================================================
  SpeciesStartingGear_Tuning.xml             Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-11
  ============================================================================

  THE OBSERVATION
  ===============
  Every Star Wars species spawned through Outer Rim's test-colony pawnkind
  arrives dressed as a modern civilian, and most of them are wearing a surgical
  face mask. Counted off save New Arrivals4:

      Apparel_ClothMask   54 / 76 Jawa   13 / 16 Hutt   7 / 11 Gungan
      Apparel_WarVeil     13 / 76 Jawa    1 / 16 Hutt   4 / 11 Gungan
      plus VAE_Apparel_Jeans, TankTop, Skirt, MilitaryUniform, Apron...

  A Hutt in a surgical mask and jeans is not the look.

  WHY THE PAWNKIND CANNOT STOP IT  [the interesting part]
  ======================================================
  All of these inherit OuterRimTestColonyPawnKind, which already asks for
  exactly the right thing and is being ignored:

      apparelTags                = ['IndustrialBasic']
      apparelAllowHeadgearChance = 0        << headgear should be IMPOSSIBLE
      apparelMoney               = 100~600

  Two separate things are wrong with that picture:

    1. Vanilla Apparel_ClothMask (Core, Apparel_Headgear.xml) declares NO
       <apparel><tags> at all, and no active mod patches tags onto it. Under
       stock rules it is not reachable through apparelTags in the first place.
    2. apparelAllowHeadgearChance is 0 and headgear is being fitted anyway.

  So something in the stack is bypassing pawnkind apparel generation wholesale.
  Twelve active assemblies reference PawnApparelGenerator; the standout suspect
  is co.uk.epicguru.factionloadout (Faction Loadout), whose entire purpose is
  overriding pawnkind gear, and which is live in the log. NOT YET CONFIRMED —
  see VERIFY below.

  THE APPROACH
  ============
  Rather than fight for control of the generator, use the one channel that does
  not go through it: <apparelRequired> is applied directly to the pawn. Then
  set <apparelMoney>0</apparelMoney> so the generator has no budget left to
  bolt jeans and a face mask on top.

  Both halves are needed. apparelRequired alone still leaves the random pass
  free to add the mask; apparelMoney 0 alone leaves a naked Jawa.

  THE ART ALREADY EXISTS  [verified in the active load set, 2026-08-11]
  =====================================================================
  KotOR Core (guy762.mm.kotorcore, load 569) ships the canonical outfit:

      guy762_JawaHood    "hood, heavy"    UpperHead + Mouth   tag SaV_apparel_jawa
      guy762_Robes_jawa  "robes, rustic"  Torso..Feet         tag SaV_apparel_jawa

  Coverage does not overlap, so both can be worn together.

  HUTTS WEAR NOTHING, DELIBERATELY
  ================================
  There is no Hutt garment anywhere in the load set. The two "hutt" apparel defs
  that exist are guy762_HelmetCombat_hutt and guy762_HvySuit_hutt, both tagged
  SaV_apparel_huttgoon — that is the GUARDS' armour, not the boss's clothing.
  Canonically a Hutt wears nothing, so apparelMoney 0 with no apparelRequired is
  both the correct look and the correct lore.

  SCOPE — Jawa and Hutt only
  ==========================
  The other eleven species from AlienSpawnEnablers.xml are left alone. For them
  apparelMoney 0 would mean naked, which is wrong, and there is no researched
  outfit to require yet. They are dev-spawn scaffolding; dressing them properly
  is a separate job that needs a costume decision per species.

  ⚠️ BLAST RADIUS. Op 1 edits the `RSW_Jawa` pawnkind itself, not a copy,
  so it changes every Jawa this pawnkind ever produces, including any the world
  generates later. That is intended — we want Jawa in robes everywhere — but it is
  wider than a Jawa_Patches-only change and should be said out loud.
  🔴 The target was `OuterRim_Jawa` until 2026-08-19 and that def NO LONGER EXISTS:
  switching the donors off renamed it, the op matched nothing, and the Jawa
  starting-gear tuning was silently not applying. The ops name the live kind now.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Both ops are PatchOperationConditional and self-disable if the field is
  already present, so an Outer Rim update that ships its own apparelRequired
  wins instead of being fought.

  Jawa_Patches loads last (562 of 562) and Outer Rim GD is 556, so the target
  exists by the time we patch it.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
    * Spawn Jawa: hood + rustic robes, and NOTHING else. No jeans, no mask.
    * Spawn Hutts: unclothed.
    * If a face mask STILL appears on either, apparelMoney 0 was overridden too,
      which confirms an assembly is driving apparel generation. Faction Loadout
      is then the first place to look, and the fix moves to its config rather
      than to XML.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       1. Jawa: hood and robes, nothing else
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="RSW_Jawa"]/apparelRequired</xpath>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="RSW_Jawa"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <apparelRequired>
          <li>guy762_Robes_jawa</li>
          <li>guy762_JawaHood</li>
        </apparelRequired>
        <apparelMoney>0</apparelMoney>
      </value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       2. Hutts wear nothing
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Jawa_Spawn_Hutt"]/apparelMoney</xpath>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Jawa_Spawn_Hutt"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <apparelMoney>0</apparelMoney>
      </value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
